<hr />
<span id="Trebuemye-pakety"></span><h4 class="subsection">6.1.2 Требуемые пакеты</h4>

<p>Activating a profile essentially boils down to exporting a bunch of
environmental variables.  This is the role of the &lsquo;<samp>etc/profile</samp>&rsquo; within
the profile.
</p>
<p><em>Note: Only the environmental variables of the packages that consume them
will be set.</em>
</p>
<p>For instance, &lsquo;<samp>MANPATH</samp>&rsquo; won&rsquo;t be set if there is no consumer
application for man pages within the profile.  So if you need to
transparently access man pages once the profile is loaded, you&rsquo;ve got two
options:
</p>
<ul>
<li> Either export the variable manually, e.g.
<div class="example">
<pre class="example">export MANPATH=/path/to/profile${MANPATH:+:}$MANPATH
</pre></div>

</li><li> Or include &lsquo;<samp>man-db</samp>&rsquo; to the profile manifest.
</li></ul>

<p>The same is true for &lsquo;<samp>INFOPATH</samp>&rsquo; (you can install &lsquo;<samp>info-reader</samp>&rsquo;),
&lsquo;<samp>PKG_CONFIG_PATH</samp>&rsquo; (install &lsquo;<samp>pkg-config</samp>&rsquo;), etc.
</p>
</div>



